<html>
  <head>
    <meta http-equiv="Content-Type" content="text/html; charset=Cp1252">
    <meta name="generator" content="Helen">
    <link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="../../../../javahelp.css">
    <title>Creating a node</title>
  </head>
  <body bgcolor="#ffffff">
    <h1>
       <img border="0" hspace="0" s7starttagpos="271" height="32" width="32" src=
      "../../../../images/carmenHelpIcons/c3_32.gif">&nbsp;&nbsp; Creating a node
    </h1>
    <table border="1" cellpadding="4" cellspacing="0" bordercolor="#000000" width="487">
      <col width="234">
      <col width="235">
      <tr>
        <td colspan="2" valign="top" width="477">
          <p align="justify">
             <b>Use case: Creating a node</b>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td colspan="2" valign="top" width="477">
          <p align="justify">
             <b>Comment:</b> Although there are three types of nodes in the program the process of
            creation is the same for all three. The difference is that it will create a certain
            type of node depending on the type of editing.
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td colspan="2" valign="top" width="477">
          <p align="justify">
             <b>Actor: User</b>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="234">
          <p align="justify">
             <b>Normal course</b>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="235">
          <p align="justify">
             <b>Alternative courses</b>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="234">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">1.When the type of editing is the creation of nodes (any type), the
            user presses with the left mouse button, without pressing any key, on the empty
            background of the network that is being edited.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="235">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3"><br>
            </font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="234">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">2.The application creates a visual node, with all the default fields,
            whose type is the type of editing.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="235">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3"><br>
            </font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="234">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">3.The node has on its properties a probability table empty, because
            there are not statements at the time of creation, and do not have any parent node
            associated.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="235">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3"><br>
            </font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="234">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">4.A new point to undo and redo the node creation is created.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="235">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3"><br>
            </font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="234">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">5.The use case <i>Updating menus when modifying a network</i> is
            executed.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="235">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3"><br>
            </font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="234">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">6.The network is marked as modified (if it was not already), placing an
            asterisk at the title of the window in which is being editing.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="235">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3"><br>
            </font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="234">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">7.If the node has been created outside the boundaries of the network
            panel, it will enlarge itself to completely accommodate the new node.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="235">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="2"><br>
            </font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
    </table>
    <p>
       &nbsp;
    </p>
  </body>
</html>
